  <Document>
    <name>🌫️ LIVE AIR QUALITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> Oct 7, 2026 6:04AM EDT</p><h2>LIVE AIR QUALITY</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/air_quality/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>PM2.5 concentration in micrograms per cubic meter (CAMS model analysis, fixed EPA-anchored scale): <b>LOWEST 0</b> green good &rarr; <b>12 moderate</b> yellow &rarr; <b>35.4 unhealthy for sensitive groups</b> orange &rarr; <b>55.4 unhealthy</b> red &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 150</b> purple very unhealthy (above clamps into purple). Same concentration always shows the same color. Modeled PM2.5 — not aerosol optical depth, not station observations.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: ECMWF CAMS European air-quality analysis via Open-Meteo Air Quality API (PM2.5, no key, hourly)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
